BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PA Day Workshop: Science of Magic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T170000
UID:6adf9de529c3d600333286dd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Spend your PA Day at the library with this fun science worksho
 p. Astonish and amaze! Children explore how magicians use perception\, as
 sumptions\, and clever science to entertain. They’ll uncover optical ill
 usions\, hidden compartments\, sleight-of-hand\, and polymer tricks while 
 learning the science behind the magic in this hands-on\, mind-bending adve
 nture with Mad Science.\nFor ages 6-12.\nDrop-in. Space is limited to the 
 first 30 participants.
LOCATION:Victoria Village\, Program Room\, downstairs.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adf9de529c3d600333286dd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
