BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Penguins: The Adventures of Pimba and family
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T170000
UID:6ae1f9ebad40276591555227@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover more about penguin biology\, ecology\, and migration 
 in this presentation of a collection of photographs taken during an MSc re
 search exchange at the Punta Tombo Penguin Reserve in Patagonia\, Argentin
 a.\nThe photographs are accompanied by the story of Pimba\, a penguin who 
 migrates with her family from Patagonia to Brazil by following ocean curre
 nts. Through Pimba’s journey\, children are introduced to the penguin li
 fe cycle in an engaging and accessible way\, using real scientific researc
 h brought to life through storytelling and images.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae1f9ebad40276591555227
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
