BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Forest of Reading  Kick-Off
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T163000
UID:6ac57fd89dbc2b002c8cce18@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Forest of Reading is Canada’s largest recreational readi
 ng program. This year\, kids at the S. Walter Stewart branch can participa
 te by reading the nominated books and voting in the Silver Birch Express A
 ward category. Kids will read at home over the fall and winter months\, wi
 th semi-regular meetups at the library before voting in April.\nAt this fi
 rst meeting\, kids will do fun activities while learning about the nominat
 ed titles and how to access them. Parents are encouraged to attend with th
 eir children wherever possible.\nThe Silver Birch Express Award is targete
 d at children who are aged 8-10\, or at the grade 3 or 4 level. Any childr
 en reading at that grade level or with the help of an adult are welcome to
  participate. Drop in.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac57fd89dbc2b002c8cce18
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
