UID:6ad7d477901b02002cc3dfe3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore the different ways organisms move (and moved) around o
 n Planet Earth. Some walk\, some swim\, and others fly. Can you tell which
  is which? Participants will be able to handle\, study and learn about str
 ange objects: fossils\, replicas and modern specimens. They will be guided
  all through the how\, when and why these organisms adapted to move as the
 y do. Interactive\, entertaining and educational\, join us for a journey i
 n living locomotion.\nRegistration is required.\nPlease only register the 
 children that will be participating\, accompanying adults do not need to r
 egister.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
