BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Literacy Jeopardy!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T170000
UID:6adbac099dbc2b002c9091bc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this digital literacy program (for kids 8+)\, participants
  will work in teams to answer Jeopardy-style questions!\nCategories will i
 nclude:\nDigital Literacy 101\nOnline Safety (privacy\, cyberbullying\, on
 line ethics\, etc)\nFake News\nBalanced Screen Time (stats\, mental health
 \, etc.)\nCool Concepts (cool\, futuristic things with digital lit e.g.\, 
 AI).\nThere will be five questions ranging from 100 to 500 points for each
  category\, as well as tiebreaker questions at the end. Have fun learning 
 about these important topics while playing this Jeopardy-style game!\nThis
  is a program for families & kids aged 8+.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
