SUMMARY:Discovery Club: Sew Your Own Garland
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T170000
UID:6ad7bb1af4d1423e2ce3e7a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 9 to 12.\nLearn some introductory hand-sewing skills 
 and make your own felt and ribbon garland! Learn stitches like the running
  stitch\, back stitch\, and blanket stitch and put together some cute orna
 ments in the shape of hearts\, stars\, snowflakes and more. In this progra
 m\, you will make 6 ornaments and stitch them together to make your very o
 wn garland.\nThis is a 6-week program and participants are recommended to 
 attend all 6 sessions.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal infor
 mation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the P
 ublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information 
 will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalua
 tion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dire
 cted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yong
 e Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7bb1af4d1423e2ce3e7a4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
