BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Snap Circuits for Kids
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T170000
UID:6aa445f9101eb7003f2f53ba@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For children ages\n8 to 12\n.\nLight up your imagination! In t
 his hands-on workshop\, young engineers will explore the basics of electri
 city and electronics using Snap Circuits. We'll learn how to build simple 
 circuits to power lights\, make sounds\, and more. Participants will work 
 in pairs to construct projects from the Snap Circuits blueprints. No prior
  experience is needed—just bring your curiosity!\nDrop in. No registrati
 on required\, but space is limited.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa445f9101eb7003f2f53ba
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
