BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ukulele Workshop for Kids
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T150000
UID:6ad652c4de300e00451b6f8e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 8 to 12.\n​Have fun learning a new instrument - the
  ukulele! This workshop will cover fundamentals of ukulele playing: the pa
 rts of a ukulele\, tuning\, strumming patterns\, and some basic chords. By
  the end of this class\, you'll have learned the skills you need to start 
 playing your first songs on the ukulele! Beginner friendly\, no previous e
 xperience is necessary.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad652c4de300e00451b6f8e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovery Club: Sew Your Own Garland
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T170000
UID:6ad7bb1af4d1423e2ce3e7a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 9 to 12.\nLearn some introductory hand-sewing skills 
 and make your own felt and ribbon garland! Learn stitches like the running
  stitch\, back stitch\, and blanket stitch and put together some cute orna
 ments in the shape of hearts\, stars\, snowflakes and more. In this progra
 m\, you will make 6 ornaments and stitch them together to make your very o
 wn garland.\nThis is a 6-week program and participants are recommended to 
 attend all 6 sessions.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal infor
 mation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the P
 ublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information 
 will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalua
 tion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dire
 cted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yong
 e Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7bb1af4d1423e2ce3e7a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
