BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Parent/Child Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T193000
UID:6a7771be4523092f0035b767@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 9 to 12 with a parent.  Please register ONCE for yo
 ur pair (child and caregiver).\nShare the love of reading as members of ou
 r book club for kids and parents! Read a book together\, then join us once
  a month at the library to chat about the book. Was it a great read? Or a 
 total stinker? All opinions and thoughts are welcome and appreciated.\nThi
 s is a monthly program and we strongly encourage book club members to com
 mit to attending all sessions through the school year.\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7771be4523092f0035b767
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
