BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T170000
UID:6a848f4e2f41840bbfc2ebdc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! Drop in. For ages 6-12\n.\nSnacks are offered during the After Scho
 ol Club for participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are g
 enerously supported\, in part\, by donors.\nTuesdays\nNovember 3rd - 24th\
 nJoin us for a series of free Artists in the Library dance workshops host
 ed by EILERS Dance Theatre!  Nov 24th will feature a performance of "Fanc
 y Cat" a dance-theatre musical for children.  The performance follows a 
 gender-expansive Grade 3 student navigating belonging\, self-expression an
 d friendship.  Performance will start at 4pm followed by an optional inte
 ractive workshop!\nTuesday\nDec. 1st\nJoin us for "Democracy Fitness: Curi
 osity". Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active particip
 ant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive session. Democracy Fit
 ness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring how peopl
 e participate in civic life\, build understanding and work together.\nGene
 rously supported by: McConnell Foundation.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a848f4e2f41840bbfc2ebdc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
