BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scratch Coding For Kids & Teens (Ages 8 -17)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T170000
UID:6ae0a6cb29c3d6003332af2e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn Scratch coding and create your own game!\nKids & teens
  will have the opportunity to learn the basics of block coding through cr
 eating a simple game using Scratch's intuitive click-and-drag interface.
 \nNo prior coding experience is required. This series is perfect for thos
 e who are curious about coding and want to dive into the exciting world of
  technology.\nParticipants are required to have basic computer skills (e.
 g.\, using a mouse\, typing on a keyboard).\nComputers will be provided f
 or this class.\nRegistration is required. Space is limited.\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
 he Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\
 , 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progr
 am registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library
  handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerli
 ne@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Digital Innovation Hub\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae0a6cb29c3d6003332af2e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sugar Skull Painting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T180000
UID:6ae0e1e49dbc2b002c915eb5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Let's celebrate life with Day of the Dead! A Mexican tradition
  where death is not mourned\, but life is loudly and joyfully celebrated.\
 nJoin us in painting a sugar skull using acrylic paint!\nFor children ages
  6+\n.\nRegistration opens November 1st at tpl.ca\nInformation Collection 
 Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto
  Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, 
 and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registr
 ation\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles y
 our information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\
 n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Kennedy/Eglinton
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae0e1e49dbc2b002c915eb5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:​Wildlife Activity Stations with Toronto Wildlife Centre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T123000
UID:6ae1160d9dbc2b002c917619@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Wildlife Centre (TWC) staff will deliver a program fo
 cused on coexistence with wildlife for children ages 5 to 12 years and the
 ir parents/caregivers.\nThere is a limit of 25 Children for this program.\
 nCaregivers are welcome to attend but online registration should be for c
 hildren only.\nThis hands-on program gives participants the opportunity to
  visit up to 4 wildlife-themed stations led by TWC staff and volunteers. C
 hildren spend 20 minutes at each station in groups exploring props and oth
 er materials\, learning unique information about wildlife and the issues a
 ffecting them.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bridlewood\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae1160d9dbc2b002c917619
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
